==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because of the high magnifications on the Master A, you will never be able to reach him with anything that has less range than he does. Make sure your units all have 500+ range, units such as [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] will actually be a massive help on this stage overall. If you want to play it extra safe, bring [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] along to pin the Master A at the base, and slowly chip away at it using a wave or piercing unit such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]. This way, as long as you bring units to counter the Zrocos and Relic Doges (Such as units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]).

==Trivia==
*Pasta Desert is an anagram of [[Tapas Desert]], the stage this is a remake of.

